            <folder name="[CT3] Care Responsibility Transition" id="id-eb7d6edc6b1d43c1a783192867f7416b">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Care Responsibility Transition" id="id-e18ec168543758bf92bf61b2a0edf5b2">
                <documentation>Establish and coordinate who has actually assumed applicable care responsibility.

Care Responsibility Transition establishes who has actually assumed applicable care responsibility and coordinates that transition. Its purpose is to prevent physical movement or exchanged information from being mistaken for accountable acceptance. It gives care continuity a responsibility meaning that a transport checkpoint or delivered referral cannot establish alone.

**Boundary**

Patient arrival, message receipt and departure do not by themselves demonstrate accepted responsibility.</documentation>
