            <folder name="[CT3] Patient Movement Coordination" id="id-342cb96683ea4ce6b215f6788e3add8b">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Patient Movement Coordination" id="id-b224448612cb5d62bbce730c2a84fb08">
                <documentation>Coordinate physical patient transit and applicable mobility constraints.

Patient Movement Coordination concerns the person's physical transit and the mobility constraints relevant to it. Within care-support logistics it supports movement appropriate to the patient's circumstances without treating transport completion as a clinical transition. Its responsibility is useful wherever care requires a change of physical location.

**Boundary**

Transport progression does not establish clinical handover, destination acceptance of care or authority over the clinical plan.</documentation>
