        <folder name="[CT1] Clinical Quality, Safety &amp; Improvement" id="id-8dfbd9ec5c4340e98d386105fdaafd28">
          <folder name="[CT2] Clinical Quality Management" id="id-b9cdc67ed5a044c0b2522e2cb13fabe7">
            <folder name="[CT3] Clinical Quality Criteria Management" id="id-e9340f71778f406dab2907f427930539">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Clinical Quality Criteria Management" id="id-f913c25edca8547fa47e0a6382936f18">
                <documentation>Establish and manage measures, indicators, expectations and criteria against which clinical quality is considered.

Clinical Quality Criteria Management establishes the measures, indicators and expectations used to consider clinical quality. It makes the basis of a later judgement explicit so that evidence can be assessed against an identifiable expectation rather than an unstated standard. Criteria are distinct from the measurements or findings produced when they are applied.

**Boundary**

Managing criteria does not originate the underlying evidence or establish a quality conclusion.</documentation>
