        <folder name="[CT1] Community Health &amp; Wellbeing" id="id-0edf3365e9a341509dd304375755131c">
          <folder name="[CT2] Preventative Health" id="id-9aaafb705c5f494ca086051f2453a653">
            <folder name="[CT3] Preventative Health Cohort Management" id="id-ee5c8093f2364ea696e43c4a4f9d0cc9">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Preventative Health Cohort Management" id="id-d328fb8f811d551699099f3f2a6e1f43">
                <documentation>Establish and manage the target population, inclusion/exclusion criteria, membership, stratification and applicable entry/exit context.

Preventative Health Cohort Management establishes who belongs to the population targeted for a preventative purpose. Inclusion, exclusion, stratification and entry or exit context make membership explainable rather than a list detached from its rationale. It provides a governed population context through which programme activity and reporting can be understood.

**Boundary**

A population at risk is not automatically a defined cohort, and cohort membership is not an individual clinical determination.</documentation>
