            <folder name="[CT3] Preventative Health Problem Identification" id="id-451a9c7becb34c5b93a2eb60183af7d8">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Preventative Health Problem Identification" id="id-f53321c902e4521ba2fd87e1b18260c1">
                <documentation>Identify and characterise a preventative-health problem warranting organised attention.

This capability establishes the preventative-health problem warranting organised attention. It gives an intended programme a reason grounded in the concern being addressed rather than assuming that a population statistic already defines the response. The identified problem can frame subsequent cohort and programme considerations without becoming an individual's clinical diagnosis.

**Boundary**

Population evidence informs problem identification but does not by itself establish a programme, cohort or individual care need.</documentation>
