            <folder name="[CT3] Diagnostic Specimen Management" id="id-8a6fc8ad92cf41eba2ba1b4f43ce7305">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Diagnostic Specimen Management" id="id-2639d5cab85d50eea6e13b397f9255d6">
                <documentation>Maintain a specimen’s identity, integrity, suitability, custody and applicable lifecycle context.

Diagnostic Specimen Management preserves the specimen context needed to trust its use: which specimen it is, whether it remains suitable, and how integrity and custody are maintained. It concerns the physical diagnostic subject across its applicable lifecycle rather than only the results generated from it. This distinction protects the relationship between evidence and the material from which it arose.

**Boundary**

Specimen stewardship is separate from diagnostic-data management and interpretation of results.</documentation>
