        <folder name="[CT1] Health Information &amp; Knowledge Management" id="id-9a81e63b185147f1a5ab5a8b1eb9fd87">
          <folder name="[CT2] Clinical Knowledge Management" id="id-0725c6fce2734b848eeb06993f30515b">
            <folder name="[CT3] Clinical Knowledge Concept Association" id="id-31ccad77d2fa4fb2b8be5c33b4851f3b">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Clinical Knowledge Concept Association" id="id-92984a7de06f57be9eaf2713871c5e03">
                <documentation>Associate knowledge with applicable governed clinical concepts without acquiring concept authority.

Clinical Knowledge Concept Association relates reusable knowledge to the governed clinical concepts relevant to its meaning. It makes the semantic context of the knowledge intelligible without allowing local association to redefine the referenced concepts. The association assists interpretation while preserving the distinction between knowledge authority and concept authority.

**Boundary**

Associating knowledge with a terminology concept does not acquire terminology governance or establish approval of the knowledge.</documentation>
