                <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--clinical-knowledge-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:677,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Clinical Knowledge Concept Association | Associate knowledge with applicable governed clinical concepts without acquiring concept authority. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--clinical-knowledge-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:670,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Clinical Knowledge Management; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--clinical-knowledge-management&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:681,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Source identified ≠ extracted material ≠ formulated knowledge ≠ reviewed/approved knowledge ≠ publication ≠ individual application. Reusable knowledge differs from source health information and individual clinical facts. Formulation is distinct from Health Information Structure Management and does not establish approval. Concept association does not redefine terminology or semantic authority. Publication establishes neither individual applicability nor a clinical conclusion/decision. Clinical knowledge and source provenance/authority remain distinguishable; no mandatory knowledge workflow is prescribed.&quot;}]"/>
