        <folder name="[CT1] Health Products &amp; Clinical Technology" id="id-128a6109487546329c22e27248daaf86">
          <folder name="[CT2] Clinical Technology Management" id="id-b2ef9eb66365409980ad50b280332e56">
            <folder name="[CT3] Clinical Device Data Integration" id="id-86bdb8172fb94dac98f84ff293c73af8">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Clinical Device Data Integration" id="id-36db1e018d39579e86ed2a2d638ffafc">
                <documentation>Acquire, exchange or convey device data through established integration capability.

Clinical Device Data Integration acquires, exchanges or conveys device data using an established integration capability. It represents actual information participation rather than the prior configuration enabling it. The distinction makes it possible to preserve the device and care context of received data while retaining separate responsibility for its subsequent interpretation.

**Boundary**

Data movement does not confer clinical meaning, originating authority or device-maintenance responsibility.</documentation>
