        <folder name="[CT1] Health Rights, Advocacy &amp; Participation" id="id-433cf3100e824adfbb049294dec7ef89">
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Health Rights, Advocacy &amp; Participation" id="id-59fb57e93d695a5781569d5fb185fdc4">
            <documentation>Protecting patient rights, facilitating informed consent, managing advance care directives, supporting patient advocacy, and enabling consumer participation in health decisions.

This capability represents the organisation's responsibility to protect patients' rights and enable their voice in health decisions. Consent, advance care directives, advocacy and consumer participation concern the legitimacy and personal consequences of care, rather than merely the availability of clinical information. The governed model retains this broad enterprise responsibility without an established subordinate capability set.

**Intent**

Support informed participation and respect for the individual's rights in decisions affecting their health.

**Boundary**

Recording a directive or restricting access can support rights without performing advocacy or managing consumer participation.

**Harmonia Architectural Relevance**

The established Adjacent classification reflects the use and supply of consent and record-access evidence. It does not assign the underlying rights, advocacy or participation activity to Harmonia.</documentation>
            <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="capability:health-rights-advocacy--participation"/>
            <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-health-rights-advocacy-participation"/>
