          <folder name="[CT2] Health Service Alignment" id="id-2d1004c33cfe4fa4af149876caf95c69">
            <folder name="[CT3] Health Service Co-Dependency Management" id="id-66d5a3122acd4c8a93f5f79ad203f529">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Health Service Co-Dependency Management" id="id-0259bdd793d65f3186810f502b700ee6">
                <documentation>Identify and manage what the service needs from others and what others need from it.

Health Service Co-Dependency Management identifies and manages reciprocal needs between a service and its wider ecosystem. It makes explicit both what the service requires from others and what others rely on it to provide. This supports alignment by exposing dependencies that a service description considered in isolation may conceal.

**Boundary**

Recognising a dependency does not acquire the provider's responsibility or establish a new technical Service dependency.</documentation>
