                <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:899,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Health Service Co-Dependency Management | Identify and manage what the service needs from others and what others need from it. |&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:895,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Decomposition assertion:** Each named child in this table is a CT3 Business Capability whose immediate CT2 parent is Health Service Alignment; that CT2 has the CT1 parent stated above.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:904,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Alignment does not establish the authoritative service catalogue; it positions the service within the environment represented by that catalogue. Modelling determines what service is needed; alignment determines how it fits; Offering Management establishes the identifiable offering. Expected future Service Catalogue richness explains architectural relevance, but establishes neither a BEC identity/hierarchy nor a BC↔BEC mapping. Alignment does not resolve operational-readiness ancestry.&quot;}]"/>
