              <property key="v0.2 / Source Locators" value="[{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:889,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;##### CT2 — Health Service Alignment&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:891,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Tier and ancestry:** CT2; parent Health Service Direction &amp; Stewardship (CT1).&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:893,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Definition:** Position the service coherently in its wider health-service ecosystem.&quot;},{&quot;anchor&quot;:&quot;ct2--health-service-alignment&quot;,&quot;line&quot;:904,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;business&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Alignment does not establish the authoritative service catalogue; it positions the service within the environment represented by that catalogue. Modelling determines what service is needed; alignment determines how it fits; Offering Management establishes the identifiable offering. Expected future Service Catalogue richness explains architectural relevance, but establishes neither a BEC identity/hierarchy nor a BC↔BEC mapping. Alignment does not resolve operational-readiness ancestry.&quot;}]"/>
