        <folder name="[CT1] Health Service Governance" id="id-42350440e9cc4efdab961dae3bbd3026">
          <folder name="[CT2] Compliance Governance" id="id-ab4ac89b18a94585afe50ed1151e9678">
            <folder name="[CT3] Compliance Assessment Definition" id="id-5ef4922e60084bf7bffac9932d517294">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Compliance Assessment Definition" id="id-a461b1332b2f5a05b6a98cc88a36bdc9">
                <documentation>Define the evidence, measures, criteria, controls and assessment arrangements sufficient to evaluate compliance with established obligations, authorities and constraints.

Compliance Assessment Definition specifies the evidence, measures, criteria and arrangements sufficient to evaluate adherence. It makes the assessment basis explicit after obligations, authorities and constraints have been established. This preserves the distinction between defining what compliance means and determining whether the available evidence demonstrates it in a particular case.

**Boundary**

Assessment definition does not replace the authoritative obligation, perform assurance or establish a compliance finding.</documentation>
