          <folder name="[CT2] Individual Care Review" id="id-ec0b8507cf4f4980830a5ce249bfe1aa">
            <folder name="[CT3] Care Appropriateness Review" id="id-eb8b2552ee85496ca870017e968b7f58">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Care Appropriateness Review" id="id-dfa6322afd30598fb230e2d13f063d12">
                <documentation>Evaluate whether the current intended care remains suitable in the individual’s current context.

Care Appropriateness Review evaluates whether the current care intent remains suitable for the individual in their present context. Its question concerns continuing suitability rather than whether treatment has produced a measurable effect. That distinction permits a review to recognise that effective care may no longer be appropriate to continue.

**Boundary**

An appropriateness judgement can identify a need to reconsider care; establishing revised intent remains Individual Care Planning.</documentation>
