            <folder name="[CT3] Health State Monitoring" id="id-737d8af425e54394873f9ea7ad54de03">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Health State Monitoring" id="id-7b61bd19dedf5e5aa7be430196c5573b">
                <documentation>Establish an aggregate, temporally situated view of the individual’s health from applicable monitored data.

Health State Monitoring brings applicable monitored data into an aggregate view situated in time. Its purpose is to make the individual's changing or stable health state intelligible across observations, rather than leaving each observation isolated. Within monitoring it provides the broader view that can also be considered in relation to a particular treatment or condition.

**Boundary**

Aggregation is not clinical interpretation. Care Response Monitoring uses the established view rather than independently recreating it.</documentation>
