            <folder name="[CT3] Population Health Reporting" id="id-6c0c5842568c49e09c0a3df7cd968946">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Population Health Reporting" id="id-9c26415a3cfa59b9ae69b8d20d381651">
                <documentation>Communicate established population-health assessments, surveillance, events, trends and findings.

Population Health Reporting communicates established assessments, surveillance findings, events and trends. Its role is to make population understanding available with its scope intact, rather than replace the assessment or event-identification work underlying it. This supports use of the findings by other abilities without assuming what those abilities must conclude.

**Boundary**

General reporting is distinct from formal notification management and does not establish a response or planning decision.</documentation>
