            <folder name="[CT3] Population Health Surveillance Management" id="id-a6d1f098fa6240aba4532e34a4734d48">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Population Health Surveillance Management" id="id-d3163fc8744d5fd7adaa99e77c9e8424">
                <documentation>Establish and manage surveillance purposes, populations, concerns and regimes.

Population Health Surveillance Management establishes the purposes, populations and regimes under which surveillance operates. It concerns the organised basis for watching health concerns, rather than any particular event detected through that activity. Keeping the regime distinct from its findings makes it possible to understand why evidence is being collected and considered.

**Boundary**

Managing surveillance neither identifies every significant event nor determines the operational response to one.</documentation>
