        <folder name="[CT1] Security, Privacy &amp; Digital Trust" id="id-2d21bf5ed5f74242b4d1a337a3266fb2">
          <folder name="[CT2] Digital Accountability &amp; Trust" id="id-008da936094644ee8b3de838677dc587">
            <folder name="[CT3] Governed Activity Attribution" id="id-2c3fcfb71f684301ade769d33ca89c25">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Governed Activity Attribution" id="id-d065c2e07dad59eca48c9e60169c0b27">
                <documentation>Preserve who participated, what was done, the attributable person/role/unit/organisation capacity and applicable permission/authority/constraint context.

Governed Activity Attribution preserves who participated and in what acting capacity, together with the relevant permission, authority and constraint context. It makes conduct explainable beyond a bare actor identifier and timestamp. Within Digital Accountability &amp; Trust, this supplies the contextual record needed to distinguish participation from entitlement.

**Boundary**

Attributing an action to a person or role does not establish that the action was permitted or appropriate.</documentation>
                <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:governed-activity-attribution"/>
                <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BC-governed-activity-attribution"/>
                <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="cap:bc-governed-activity-attribution"/>
