            <folder name="[CT3] Security &amp; Information-Use Accountability" id="id-f6457f9c1fc546979e4244b1de2c8444">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Security &amp; Information-Use Accountability" id="id-8e1cc85a4269529bb99d74f1f6ebe1cf">
                <documentation>Evaluate whether attributed security-relevant activity/information use was appropriate within policy, obligation and authority constraints, and establish accountability.

This capability evaluates attributed activity and information use against applicable policy, obligations and authority constraints. It establishes accountability rather than simply recording participation. Its purpose depends on preserving the circumstances of action so that appropriateness is considered within the relevant mandate instead of inferred from identity or technical success.

**Boundary**

An authenticated actor and a successful operation are not proof of legitimate information use.</documentation>
