          <folder name="[CT2] Digital Identity &amp; Access Governance" id="id-3da01c058dfb4036b274ed5542b8c9ce">
            <folder name="[CT3] Access Control Assurance &amp; Reporting" id="id-74debfb18b5d4b5795ee2672aec766e4">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Access Control Assurance &amp; Reporting" id="id-de17cc6571dc50e688259ca76c68c889">
                <documentation>Establish organisational assurance/evidence of whether access-control arrangements are appropriately established and operating.

This capability establishes organisational evidence and assurance about whether access-control arrangements are appropriately established and operating. It makes control effectiveness a distinct concern from defining requirements or performing an individual enforcement action. Reporting communicates that established position without making an isolated successful check proof of end-to-end control.

**Boundary**

Subject-specific access-control assurance does not create another macro-level Health Service Assurance hierarchy.</documentation>
