            <folder name="[CT3] Access Control Enforcement" id="id-1c9120ec71c44488babcf7a6e287323b">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Access Control Enforcement" id="id-03315366be1a58acbacd027ab32bf8bf">
                <documentation>Ensure physical, procedural and digital control mechanisms coherently impose intended controls.

Access Control Enforcement ensures that intended controls are coherently imposed through the applicable physical, procedural and digital mechanisms. It represents the organisational ability to make controls effective, rather than equating enforcement with one software decision. Its outcome depends on the controlled circumstances and the arrangements intended to apply there.

**Boundary**

A local software authorisation result alone does not establish coherent end-to-end organisational enforcement.</documentation>
