            <folder name="[CT3] Identity Assurance" id="id-b506161df5c8488aa03df2922ef73e0e">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Identity Assurance" id="id-a5df034d251455f0aba1de9817628801">
                <documentation>Establish sufficient confidence that a person is who they claim to be through appropriate evidence and processes.

Identity Assurance establishes confidence that a person is who they claim to be using appropriate evidence and processes. It concerns the basis and strength of the identity claim, rather than only successful use of an authentication mechanism. Within identity governance it makes confidence a question that can be considered separately from contextual sufficiency and access authority.

**Boundary**

An assured identity is not automatically sufficient for every context or permitted to perform every action.</documentation>
