            <folder name="[CT3] Terminology Localisation" id="id-ddd258e4ced14110b19bfae45689e638">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Terminology Localisation" id="id-4ac46da5b1d157f5b20e48a42e1bed53">
                <documentation>Manage controlled local responses where adopted terminology does not meet legitimate organisational semantic requirements.

Terminology Localisation manages controlled local responses where adopted terminology does not satisfy legitimate organisational semantic needs. It makes the local variation explicit rather than allowing ad hoc usage to conceal a gap or change in meaning. Within clinical-semantics governance, this preserves a distinction between governed local adaptation and uncontrolled drift.

**Boundary**

The established localisation responsibility concerns terminology; no corresponding Classification Localisation capability is inferred.</documentation>
