          <folder name="[CT2] Health Information Standards Governance" id="id-7f8b4196668a484cb3a003c2279043c8">
            <folder name="[CT3] Information Model Adoption" id="id-acf84c3841b0424985ef0576f3744d7e">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Information Model Adoption" id="id-d80607019cdb5e819abe227279c0f20e">
                <documentation>Adopt applicable information models, including intrinsic assessment of adoption impacts.

Information Model Adoption establishes the organisation's use of an applicable information model, including consideration of the consequences of adopting it. It gives a discovered model an organisational standing distinct from mere availability. The intrinsic impact consideration helps adoption remain a business governance responsibility rather than a mechanical import of definitions.

**Boundary**

Adoption does not perform every education, compliance or governance-oversight responsibility associated with subsequent use.</documentation>
                <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="business-capability:information-model-adoption"/>
