            <folder name="[CT3] Practitioner Qualification Management" id="id-98e6cbff24dc4c89a608f0a2b5cfddbe">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Practitioner Qualification Management" id="id-14aceb46b4575c24937a9500d6ea9492">
                <documentation>Govern professional/clinical standing and qualifications, including applicable review, escalation, complaints, penalties/issues, suspension and revocation.

Practitioner Qualification Management governs professional and clinical standing, including review and changes such as suspension or revocation. It makes qualification a continuing governed concern rather than a static directory attribute. That standing can constrain engagement and privilege while remaining distinguishable from either an employment relationship or permission for a particular activity.

**Boundary**

Qualification alone does not establish engagement, clinical privilege, device-specific enablement or operational assignment.</documentation>
