          <folder name="[CT2] Healthcare Organisation &amp; Service Structure Management" id="id-bf82fdc8c4e7414098742c9942385294">
            <folder name="[CT3] Healthcare Location Definition Management" id="id-57a68e7297154bf6aaaac97c5df8e2f0">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Healthcare Location Definition Management" id="id-c202cbbd5a9a5759bcd79a6c933da7a2">
                <documentation>Establish and manage recognised locations and their applicable business characteristics and relationships.

Healthcare Location Definition Management establishes recognised places and their business characteristics and relationships. It gives health-service activity an intelligible location context while remaining separate from maintaining the physical facilities. A defined location can be referenced in offerings and operational activity without implying that it is currently usable or ready for care.

**Boundary**

Location definition is not facilities operation, care-place readiness or service availability.</documentation>
