          <folder name="[CT3] Service Offering Readiness Coordination" id="id-d71e3b1f0ca04360b1f92689a641521f">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Service Offering Readiness Coordination" id="id-f4b94cd1b3af514eb9e99ddfd82245ba">
              <documentation>Assemble the dependency evidence needed to determine and communicate whether a defined service offering is operationally ready in a particular context.

**Overview**

Collective readiness depends on suitable workforce, spaces, equipment, materials and supporting services. This proposal evaluates their joint availability for an offering without treating one available bed, an operating-hours declaration or aggregate capacity as service readiness.

**Intent**

Distinguish collective service deliverability from nominal availability or readiness of any single dependency.

**Boundary**

Contributing capabilities retain source readiness and resource management. Clinical go/no-go decisions and service governance are not granted by this information-based coordination.</documentation>
              <property key="v0.2 / Source Capture Key" value="proposal:bec-service-offering-readiness-coordination"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Snapshot Reference ID" value="HCM-BEC-service-offering-readiness-coordination"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / LaTeX Label" value="cap:bec-service-offering-readiness-coordination"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Construct Type" value="capability"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Capability Tier" value="CT3"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Architectural Status" value="Proposed"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Record State" value="pending_adjudication"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Placement Status" value="Proposed"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Structural ID Status" value="Proposed"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Structural Canonical ID" value="CT1-BEC-CARE-OPERATIONS-COORDINATION-ENABLEMENT.CT2-BEC-CARE-RESOURCE-CAPACITY-COORDINATION.CT3-BEC-SERVICE-OFFERING-READINESS-COORDINATION"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Name Status" value="Proposed"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Architecture Identity Status" value="Unresolved — representation ID only"/>
              <property key="v0.2 / Derivation Provenance" value="{&quot;authority&quot;:&quot;Proposed only; cited source standing is not inherited&quot;,&quot;derivation&quot;:&quot;Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:[{&quot;line&quot;:403,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/02-strategy/capabilities/business-capabilities.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Available staff, equipment or an unoccupied bed does not establish usable service capacity. Available for service coverage ≠ deployed to a care requirement ≠ assigned operational work. Care Resource Deployment consumes availability, role, qualification, engagement and privilege context without changing authoritative rosters, qualifications, employment or privilege records. It establishes no Harmonia authority over clinical work, enterprise assets or hospital-wide logistics. Operational capacity is distinct from strategic/tactical capacity planning and from collective service readiness (OI-BC-002).&quot;},{&quot;line&quot;:34,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;[Context-specific Capacity Management](../behaviours/04-health-service-operations.md#capacity-management-responsibility-boundary) establishes/manages capacity meaning for Clinic &amp; Practice Operations, Ward Operations, Theatre Operations, Emergency Department Operations, Outpatient Operations and Mobile Staff Management. Their local information responsibilities express available, committed and utilised capacity without prescribing a shared formal Information Object or identical model. Bed/care-place and equipment state contribute; they do not alone establish service capacity. Service Capacity Management consumes/coordinates those capacity states; Work Allocation &amp; Dispatch and Discharge Management may consume them without acquiring their ownership. Exact provider contracts remain unestablished.&quot;}],&quot;method&quot;:&quot;AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task&quot;}"/>
