              <property key="v0.2 / Derivation Provenance" value="{&quot;authority&quot;:&quot;Proposed only; cited source standing is not inherited&quot;,&quot;derivation&quot;:&quot;Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:[{&quot;line&quot;:33,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/05-information-systems-architecture/design-notes/DesignNote-Identity-Authentication-and-Authorisation-Architecture.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Identity.Authentication is a **Separately Provided Capability (SEP)**. Harmonia's primary authentication pattern is standards-based OIDC/OAuth integration with an externally managed Identity Provider.&quot;}],&quot;method&quot;:&quot;AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task&quot;}"/>
