          <folder name="[CT2] Care Resource &amp; Capacity Coordination" id="id-c1270bff03d14190a8b292fba96ae0d8">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Care Resource &amp; Capacity Coordination" id="id-2f2df4a3cea854849a3a985fa2b47996">
              <documentation>Relate operational care-place and equipment state to the coordinated view of service demand and capacity.

**Overview**

Relate operational care-place and equipment state to the coordinated view of service demand and capacity. Its constituent abilities distinguish Bed &amp; Care-Place Management; Clinical Resource Management; Service Capacity Management.

**Intent**

Make resource-state contributions and coordinated capacity views usable without collapsing their different responsibilities.

**Boundary**

Bed/equipment availability is a contribution to capacity, not its definition. Higher-order capacity consumes local capacity without taking its ownership.</documentation>
