          <folder name="[CT2] Specialist Clinical Context Integration" id="id-428e092ff1d64462a5aafa90dbc84a67">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Specialist Clinical Context Integration" id="id-54d9ddfc96fc54b2bf9e1617c856f538">
              <documentation>Integrate specialist assessment, investigation and therapeutic information with longitudinal and episode context.

**Overview**

Integrate specialist assessment, investigation and therapeutic information with longitudinal and episode context. Its constituent abilities distinguish Clinical Assessment; Diagnostic Services; Therapeutic Services; Medication Therapy; Allied Health; Rehabilitation.

**Intent**

Keep specialised clinical context connected to the wider record while retaining the specialist source of clinical judgement.

**Boundary**

A clinical specialty is evidence for integration purpose, not authority to invent a specialist engine, clinical decision or duplicated general capture function.</documentation>
