          <folder name="[CT3] Service Availability Definition" id="id-3a1c563476534030ae91ad5b746855c7">
            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Service Availability Definition" id="id-fe6ea1fbce775529bcc7e3f9a41c2305">
              <documentation>Modeling regular operating hours, exceptional closures, and emergency availability.

**Overview**

Regular hours, on-call windows and exceptional closures describe when an offering is nominally available. They provide an input to readiness and scheduling without proving that all required dependencies are ready.

**Intent**

Express the operating windows against which a service participation request can be considered.

**Boundary**

Represents operating windows and exceptions; it does not establish staffing, capacity or readiness.</documentation>
