            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Clinical Device Administration" id="id-a6aaf19f1f225b67b1e3a19740d5f457">
              <documentation>Clinical Device Administration represents device types, identifiable instances, patient or location associations and communication endpoints. This lets device-originated information be interpreted in relation to the actual device and care context, rather than merely a network address. Type, instance, assignment and connectivity each answer a different question about the source of device data.

**Overview**

Clinical Device Administration represents device types, identifiable instances, patient or location associations and communication endpoints. This lets device-originated information be interpreted in relation to the actual device and care context, rather than merely a network address. Type, instance, assignment and connectivity each answer a different question about the source of device data.

**Intent**

Clinical Device Administration represents device types, identifiable instances, patient or location associations and communication endpoints. This lets device-originated information be interpreted in relation to the actual device and care context, rather than merely a network address. Type, instance, assignment and connectivity each answer a different question about the source of device data.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

Device registration is not maintenance, release management or clinical interpretation. An endpoint credential does not by itself authorise clinical use of the device.</documentation>
