            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Health Service Administration" id="id-19d0a7d9080e5758915878db238ec2d8">
              <documentation>Health Service Administration represents identifiable services and the conditions under which organisations, locations and practitioner roles provide them. Catalogue publishing, service-location-provider association, operating schedules and eligibility definitions allow a service to be understood as more than a location or specialty label. The service context remains material wherever activity meaning or accountability depends on it.

**Overview**

Health Service Administration represents identifiable services and the conditions under which organisations, locations and practitioner roles provide them. Catalogue publishing, service-location-provider association, operating schedules and eligibility definitions allow a service to be understood as more than a location or specialty label. The service context remains material wherever activity meaning or accountability depends on it.

**Intent**

Health Service Administration represents identifiable services and the conditions under which organisations, locations and practitioner roles provide them. Catalogue publishing, service-location-provider association, operating schedules and eligibility definitions allow a service to be understood as more than a location or specialty label. The service context remains material wherever activity meaning or accountability depends on it.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

This capability owns the service mapping associations, not the mapped organisations, locations or practitioners. The supplied Domain03-to-Domain04 trace preserves that distinction; it does not transfer entity ownership.</documentation>
