              <folder name="[Feature] Atomic Care-Place Modeling" id="id-8fd53ed65c684ad29b31e6eca46dc07d">
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Atomic Care-Place Modeling" id="id-d1125ae070df590ba4705abb33cf77ea">
                  <documentation>Define specific beds, care-bays, and examination rooms with their physical capabilities (e.g., telemetry-capable, negative-pressure).

Care-place modelling identifies the particular physical place and characteristics relevant to care, such as isolation or telemetry capability. It supplies the descriptive frame against which changing occupancy and readiness can be considered without making those states part of the place's identity.</documentation>
