            <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Organisation Administration" id="id-97a226da4bae53e9bb0cb071c6dbf5c2">
              <documentation>Organisation Administration maintains the identity, profiles, structural relationships and contact context of participating healthcare organisations. It enables a legal or operational entity to be distinguished from a department, network relationship or communication channel. This supports consistent interpretation of providers and destinations across information flows rather than allowing each interface to create an incompatible organisational account.

**Overview**

Organisation Administration maintains the identity, profiles, structural relationships and contact context of participating healthcare organisations. It enables a legal or operational entity to be distinguished from a department, network relationship or communication channel. This supports consistent interpretation of providers and destinations across information flows rather than allowing each interface to create an incompatible organisational account.

**Intent**

Organisation Administration maintains the identity, profiles, structural relationships and contact context of participating healthcare organisations. It enables a legal or operational entity to be distinguished from a department, network relationship or communication channel. This supports consistent interpretation of providers and destinations across information flows rather than allowing each interface to create an incompatible organisational account.

**Boundary**

Information administration does not confer authority over the represented person, organisation, service, place, device or clinical activity.

---

## History

### Boundary — predecessor explanation

Representing organisational structure does not acquire corporate authority or ownership of every service offered by the organisation.</documentation>
