              <property key="v0.2 / Derivation Provenance" value="{&quot;authority&quot;:&quot;Proposed only; cited source standing is not inherited&quot;,&quot;derivation&quot;:&quot;Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:[{&quot;line&quot;:626,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/02-strategy/capabilities/business-capabilities.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;| Health Service Demand Assessment | Assess current/expected health-service demand across a population, geography, service domain or health-system context. |&quot;},{&quot;line&quot;:34,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;[Context-specific Capacity Management](../behaviours/04-health-service-operations.md#capacity-management-responsibility-boundary) establishes/manages capacity meaning for Clinic &amp; Practice Operations, Ward Operations, Theatre Operations, Emergency Department Operations, Outpatient Operations and Mobile Staff Management. Their local information responsibilities express available, committed and utilised capacity without prescribing a shared formal Information Object or identical model. Bed/care-place and equipment state contribute; they do not alone establish service capacity. Service Capacity Management consumes/coordinates those capacity states; Work Allocation &amp; Dispatch and Discharge Management may consume them without acquiring their ownership. Exact provider contracts remain unestablished.&quot;}],&quot;method&quot;:&quot;AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task&quot;}"/>
