          <folder name="[CT2] Clinical Logistics Coordination" id="id-91302754014b49ae94818eab4e10c800">
            <folder name="[CT3] Specimen Metadata Management" id="id-3116d1f03ac8498b9ae85481470e6a1f">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Specimen Metadata Management" id="id-e58d7bdb27f95fb396623167a677a5ba">
                <documentation>Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen.

**Overview**

Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Manage the identifying, descriptive, custody and relevant handling information needed to interpret a transported specimen.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.</documentation>
