            <folder name="[CT3] Specimen Movement Traceability" id="id-eab3dcdd50a94da7b4b29c5a13d82b8d">
              <folder name="[Feature] Pathology Specimen Transport Tracking" id="id-3c093f11dc224a4593395fb0247a7562">
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Pathology Specimen Transport Tracking" id="id-6df39c0df1365e7390f6d062c1cdb576">
                  <documentation>Track pickup, custody chain, transport conditions, and laboratory delivery of clinical specimens.

Specimen transport tracking retains pickup, custody and condition context through laboratory delivery. It supports interpretation of the material's journey without treating a delivered package as proof of specimen suitability, completed analysis or an authorised diagnostic report.</documentation>
