          <folder name="[CT2] Theatre Operations" id="id-00c8ff30ab73489d832426222dba0245">
            <folder name="[CT3] Perioperative Logistics Coordination" id="id-bd2b6789d2554c73bdaafe4533106482">
              <folder name="[Feature] Operating Theatre Case Progression" id="id-5c405d793ae547ef8154b860150b05ab">
                <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Operating Theatre Case Progression" id="id-b0e1921663045bf5a2297d507ff219fc">
                  <documentation>Track surgical case state transitions (CALLED → IN_THEATRE → ANAESTHETISED → INCISION → CLOSED → RECOVERY).

Case progression records externally established surgical milestones in an operationally meaningful sequence. It makes the theatre situation visible without authorising or performing the clinical acts denoted by anaesthesia, incision, closure or recovery.</documentation>
