                <documentation>Manage permitted patient health-information disclosure and its applicable recipient, purpose and restriction conditions.

**Overview**

Manage permitted patient health-information disclosure and its applicable recipient, purpose and restriction conditions. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Manage permitted patient health-information disclosure and its applicable recipient, purpose and restriction conditions.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority. Client consent directives remain owned by Client Privacy Guardrail Management (FEAT-EM-09); this capability references and respects those determinations without defining a second consent owner.</documentation>
