            <folder name="[CT3] Patient Health Information Filter Management" id="id-55bd13e433de4340bcb168e34bad31d0">
              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Patient Health Information Filter Management" id="id-1174f336b2b158229d94060f3b0f43ed">
                <documentation>Manage patient health-information filtering rules and qualified projections while respecting established client privacy and consent determinations.

**Overview**

Manage patient health-information filtering rules and qualified projections while respecting established client privacy and consent determinations. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Manage patient health-information filtering rules and qualified projections while respecting established client privacy and consent determinations.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority. Client consent directives remain owned by Client Privacy Guardrail Management (FEAT-EM-09); this capability references and respects those determinations without defining a second consent owner.</documentation>
