              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Patient Health Information Restriction Management" id="id-0c99a409fcad5e30b1c384f25976197f">
                <documentation>Manage application of patient health-information restrictions using the client-associated privacy and consent responsibilities retained by Client Privacy Guardrail Management.

**Overview**

Manage application of patient health-information restrictions using the client-associated privacy and consent responsibilities retained by Client Privacy Guardrail Management. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Manage application of patient health-information restrictions using the client-associated privacy and consent responsibilities retained by Client Privacy Guardrail Management.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority. Client consent directives remain owned by Client Privacy Guardrail Management (FEAT-EM-09); this capability references and respects those determinations without defining a second consent owner.</documentation>
