                <documentation>Define the identifying, semantic and governed-use characteristics of an information asset.

**Overview**

Define the identifying, semantic and governed-use characteristics of an information asset. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Define the identifying, semantic and governed-use characteristics of an information asset.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.</documentation>
