              <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Information Product Administration" id="id-ed9226f42cd853c08bb48e6ce86cfd4b">
                <documentation>Administer identifiable governed information products, their purpose, content standing and qualified release/use context.

**Overview**

Administer identifiable governed information products, their purpose, content standing and qualified release/use context. The reviewed hierarchy assigns this enduring ability to its stated business-enabling context.

**Intent**

Administer identifiable governed information products, their purpose, content standing and qualified release/use context.

**Boundary**

Information administration and coordination preserve the authority of the responsible source, clinical actor and governed domain; they confer no additional real-world management authority.</documentation>
