                  <property key="v0.2 / Derivation Provenance" value="{&quot;authority&quot;:&quot;Proposed only; cited source standing is not inherited&quot;,&quot;derivation&quot;:&quot;Strongly implied bounded information/work responsibility&quot;,&quot;evidence&quot;:[{&quot;line&quot;:34,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/03-business-architecture/information-responsibility/information-responsibility.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;[Context-specific Capacity Management](../behaviours/04-health-service-operations.md#capacity-management-responsibility-boundary) establishes/manages capacity meaning for Clinic &amp; Practice Operations, Ward Operations, Theatre Operations, Emergency Department Operations, Outpatient Operations and Mobile Staff Management. Their local information responsibilities express available, committed and utilised capacity without prescribing a shared formal Information Object or identical model. Bed/care-place and equipment state contribute; they do not alone establish service capacity. Service Capacity Management consumes/coordinates those capacity states; Work Allocation &amp; Dispatch and Discharge Management may consume them without acquiring their ownership. Exact provider contracts remain unestablished.&quot;},{&quot;line&quot;:403,&quot;path&quot;:&quot;docs/markdown/02-strategy/capabilities/business-capabilities.md&quot;,&quot;standing&quot;:&quot;Current corpus evidence; does not promote the derived assertion&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;**Boundary:** Available staff, equipment or an unoccupied bed does not establish usable service capacity. Available for service coverage ≠ deployed to a care requirement ≠ assigned operational work. Care Resource Deployment consumes availability, role, qualification, engagement and privilege context without changing authoritative rosters, qualifications, employment or privilege records. It establishes no Harmonia authority over clinical work, enterprise assets or hospital-wide logistics. Operational capacity is distinct from strategic/tactical capacity planning and from collective service readiness (OI-BC-002).&quot;}],&quot;method&quot;:&quot;AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task&quot;}"/>
