      <folder name="[Topic] Ordering" id="id-d1a6fab9b1344b639299f7ed08cbecd5">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Ordering" id="id-939dda01afdc40eabc1bb723f9da5b7b" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information concerning formal requests for services or activities, including their intent, routing, progression, modification, contextual information and correlation with resulting information or fulfilment.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Order" id="id-a025ad6103e24c79b90f39a16b8b15a2" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information describing a formal request for a service, activity or other fulfilment to be performed, including its subject, requester, intent and requested outcome.

Harmonia enforces an essential architectural rule regarding clinical requisitions and service delivery:

$$\text{Order} \neq \text{Healthcare Service}$$

```mermaid
graph TD
    ORDER[&quot;Order&lt;br/>(Authoritative Requisition / Directive)&quot;]
    DELIV[&quot;DeliverableHealthcareService&lt;br/>(Bound Service Context)&quot;]
    DELIVERY[&quot;HealthcareServiceDelivery&lt;br/>(Information Referring to Service Execution)&quot;]

    DELIV -.->|&quot;may be requested / directed via&quot;| ORDER
    ORDER -.->|&quot;requests / directs&quot;| DELIVERY
    DELIV -->|&quot;fulfilled by&quot;| DELIVERY
```

### Key Semantics &amp; Invariants
1. **Associated Request Mechanism**: An `Order` is an authoritative clinical requisition, directive, or prescription requesting the delivery of a service. It is **NOT** a mandatory lifecycle stage of `Healthcare Service`.
2. **Delivery Without an Order**: Service delivery may legitimately occur without an `Order` where business or clinical semantics permit (e.g. *Emergency Resuscitation*, *Triage Assessment*, *Direct Routine Nursing Care*, *Scheduled Facility Maintenance*).
3. **Independent Lifecycles**: An `Order` possesses its own lifecycle states (*Requested*, *Accepted*, *In-Progress*, *Completed*, *Discontinued*), owned by `Order Administration`, distinct from the lifecycle of the service delivery itself.

Source standing: Established Package1 conceptual information meaning; residual qualifications in selected section remain unchanged.</documentation>
          <property key="canonicalId" value="2a791e0e1f6b45c0a57fb8233f73faa5"/>
          <property key="displayName" value="Order BO"/>
          <property key="friendlyName" value="OrderBo"/>
          <property key="canonicalName" value="BO-OrderBo"/>
          <property key="archimateType" value="DataObject"/>
          <property key="Baseline / Source Path" value="docs/markdown/04-information-architecture/information-families/healthcare-service.md"/>
          <property key="Baseline / Source Section" value="## 4. Associated Request Mechanism: Order"/>
          <property key="Baseline / Source SHA256" value="ea164a82844b8589b11eef33e75957293239aea5362d1ffcb404e1031736cabd"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrderChange" id="id-baee40c9809143febeb1e82bf00724ac" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>Information describing a requested modification to an existing Order, including the nature, context and disposition of the requested change.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrderContext" id="id-859e6f00b88a46b4b7647a1fe8fe946a" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>Information bringing together the subject, requester, requested activity, intended performer and other context necessary to understand and act upon an Order.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrderProgressionEvent" id="id-6215587fc627479f906c85881f1acc05" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information describing significant changes in the state and handling of an Order as it progresses from request through fulfilment or other resolution.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrderResult" id="id-ea0e962d9eb7422c910091d8de80f8a8" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information establishing the relationship between an Order and information produced as a consequence of its fulfilment.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] OrderRouting" id="id-28bf91e4dae44a3eaa32741d43368075" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information describing where and how an Order is to be directed for acceptance, processing or fulfilment.</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
      <folder name="[Topic] Enterprise" id="id-9556a8d0520d424e94ef2bbdc3e49017">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Enterprise" id="id-74f9c5df31f2430ca725c39e285cd9c3" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>Information concerning healthcare organisations and organisational units, including their identity, classification, structure, profile, relationships, and contact information.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Organisation" id="id-da6abec4c12f4e689f8e7516dfece8f1" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information describing an organisation participating in healthcare, including its identity, characteristics and role within the healthcare environment.

- **Semantic Classification**: `Entity`
- **Definition**: An identifiable legal, corporate, or administrative organisation operating within the healthcare domain (e.g. Health Service District, Hospital Network, Private Healthcare Provider, Diagnostic Laboratory Enterprise).
- **Architectural Scope**: Represents the overarching enterprise entity possessing legal identity, operational mandate, and administrative responsibility.

