      <folder name="[Topic] Place" id="id-ad1f524900564f68beaf9148efd70d4d">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] Place" id="id-e7b6552e6cd748fcae781becea007f01" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information concerning physical, geospatial, functional and care locations, including their identity, classification, spatial relationships, containment, characteristics, and care-place definitions.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="[Topic] CarePlace" id="id-2e0b4b866f6c45db8de068f6dffd409f" profiles="id-5a89cc5b58a84b449fad554acd6b9c5b">
          <documentation>**Description**
Information describing the characteristics and intended healthcare function of a place in which care may be provided, independently of its transient operational state.

- **Semantic Classification**: `Definition`
- **Definition**: The static engineering, physical infrastructure, and architectural specification of a bed bay or clinical treatment point.
- **Key Characteristics**: Physical capacity, isolation classification (e.g. *Negative Pressure*, *Positive Pressure*, *Standard*), medical gas outlet provisions (e.g. *Oxygen*, *Suction*, *Medical Air*), emergency power backup, and fixed telemetry wiring.
- **Architectural Boundary**: Captures what the physical care-place **is** built to support, independent of its transient operational occupancy.

Source standing: Established Package1 conceptual information meaning; residual qualifications in selected section remain unchanged.</documentation>
