\end{longtable}\endgroup
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Care Coordination \&amp; Transition supports continuity by keeping participation, actual responsibility assumption and discharge progression distinct. Care teams may collaborate while responsibility is shared or changes, but physical transit and information exchange do not themselves establish who has accepted care. The capability therefore addresses continuity of accountable participation as well as the practical circumstances of departure.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Coordinate care participation, actual responsibility transition and discharge.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Avoid gaps in care continuity caused by treating a movement or communication as an accepted responsibility transition.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Harmonia may assemble handover information without managing clinical handover. Arrival, discharge readiness and physical departure are not equivalent to responsibility acceptance.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Scope / Contained Elements}
