\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Preparedness asks whether the service as a whole can operate, distinct from scheduling capacity or readiness of a single place. This is a proposed missing business frame for the already identified readiness concern.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Establish whether service offerings can be delivered in their intended operating contexts through the combined standing of their dependencies.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Recognise whether the whole service can actually operate in its intended context.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Does not own the dependencies, their management or clinical execution.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Review Confidence}
Low; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:a4c0900c47c945d9]{business-capabilities.md:403}
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Scope / Contained Elements}
\begingroup\small\setlength{\TableWidth}{\dimexpr\linewidth-6\tabcolsep-4\arrayrulewidth\relax}
