\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

This capability frames professional medication provision and medication-specific advice. Prescription dispensing, non-prescription provision, advice and dose administration aids answer different needs, even where exercised by one pharmacy. The decomposition keeps the authorised regimen, provision of medicine and actual administration separate so that a supply event is not mistaken for treatment performed.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Provide professional medication/\allowbreak{}pharmacy services under applicable controls.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Support safe, professionally controlled access to and use of medication within the established pharmacy responsibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary — v0.1 explanation}

Advice does not confer prescribing authority, and dose aids do not establish a regimen. Whether specialised compounding/\allowbreak{}preparation warrants a separate capability remains unresolved under OI-BC-001.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Preserved v0.1 Review Matters}

OI-BC-001: a compounding/\allowbreak{}preparation CT3 is neither established nor rejected; do not infer subsumption.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Scope / Contained Elements}
