\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Research Information Support represents the ability to make existing health information available for a legitimate research purpose. Its single established child concentrates on governed provision, preserving the constraints under which information can be used rather than treating technical availability as research permission. The narrow decomposition reflects R1/\allowbreak{}R2 sufficiency rather than a claim to encompass every form of research support.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Provide the existing health information needed for authorised research within the deliberately bounded R1/\allowbreak{}R2 responsibility.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Support authorised research with information supplied under the applicable ethical, privacy and governance conditions.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Research governance, trial oversight and specialist analysis remain unmodelled and are not absorbed into provision.


