\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

This capability retains the financial and corporate-support context material to R1/\allowbreak{}R2. The financial branch concentrates on information about clinical activity relevant to charging or cost; corporate support covers administrative, physical, technical, people and communication conditions affecting service activity. The limited decomposition makes these dependencies visible without assigning a complete corporate enterprise architecture to Harmonia.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Provide the bounded clinical-activity charging information and enterprise support context required for R1/\allowbreak{}R2, without assigning enterprise finance, HR, facilities or ICT operating authority to Harmonia.


\cataloguefield{section}{Intent}

Support health-service activity with the required corporate context and legitimate activity information.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Evidence about cost-relevant activity does not perform billing or accounting. Consuming corporate resource state does not acquire the authority to operate those resources.


\cataloguefield{section}{Harmonia Architectural Relevance}

Clinical activity evidence provides material financial support. Corporate constraints may also affect enablement, but contextual consumption does not classify every corporate descendant as Relevant or Core.


\cataloguefield{section}{Scope / Contained Elements}
