Evidence &amp; \hyperref[rad:business:1066]{business:1068} (p.\,\pageref{rad:business:1066}); \hyperref[rad:business:1064]{business:1064} (p.\,\pageref{rad:business:1064}); \hyperref[rad:business:1071]{business:1071} (p.\,\pageref{rad:business:1071}) &amp; Source standing does not approve the derived assertion.\\\hline
\end{longtable}\endgroup
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Assurance Evidence Assessment evaluates available evidence against the established approach and criteria. It produces the assessed basis from which a legitimate conclusion may be determined, retaining qualifications and evidentiary limits. The responsibility is evaluative rather than the operational production of the source information or remediation of what it reveals.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Evaluate available evidence against the established assurance approach and criteria.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Assessment is distinct from conclusion determination; unavailable or insufficient evidence must remain explicit.


\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection{BC CT3: Assurance Conclusion Determination}
\label{cap:bc-assurance-conclusion-determination}
\index{Assurance Conclusion Determination}
\begingroup\small\setlength{\TableWidth}{\dimexpr\linewidth-6\tabcolsep-4\arrayrulewidth\relax}
\begin{longtable}{|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.2\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.48\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.32\TableWidth}|}
