\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Administer practitioner identity, professional profile and supplied registration information with its issuing-authority attribution.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Administer practitioner identity, professional profile and supplied registration information with its issuing-authority attribution.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Professional registration and profile representation do not grant clinical or operational privilege.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:140}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Identifying and verifying individual healthcare professionals.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Practitioner identity and professional profile information let care participants be recognised across organisations. Registration and profile standing remain attributed to the issuing authority, while discovery makes that described person usable in care integration.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Allow a described healthcare professional to be reliably recognised and found across participating systems.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-5BB55046}} (line 2997). Working locators are not identity aliases.
