\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Administer the identity, address, geospatial description and physical containment relationships of healthcare locations.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Administer the identity, address, geospatial description and physical containment relationships of healthcare locations.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Location description does not establish occupancy, cleanliness, service capacity or service readiness.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:177}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Identifying and profiling geographic locations, physical campuses, and health facilities.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Addresses, geospatial context and facility identity establish which physical place an information or activity concern refers to. Describing a location remains separate from deciding what services can operate there now.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Identify the physical place relevant to care information and operational activity.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Consolidated / decomposed predecessors}
\nameref{cap:bec-healthcare-location} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-healthcare-location}); \nameref{cap:bec-location-structure} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-location-structure})
