\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Encounter progression preserves the difference between planned, arrived, active, leave and discharged circumstances. These states make administrative activity interpretable without implying a clinical outcome. The source's ON\_LEAVE transition detail remains incomplete in the corresponding Process and is not repaired here.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Track encounter status transitions (\texttt{\seqsplit{PLANNED}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{ARRIVED}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{IN\_PROGRESS}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{ON\_LEAVE}} → \texttt{\seqsplit{DISCHARGED}}).


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Meaningful reviewed CT3 framing selected for the existing Feature semantics; established responsibility provenance is preserved.


