\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Consumers need to interpret prior care-place and episode relationships, not just the latest encounter state; historical retrieval remains bounded by source attribution and access policy.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition — Proposed}

Expose qualified episode, movement and encounter-history context.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Boundary}

A historical view does not retrospectively alter clinical events or acquire longitudinal-record ownership.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Meaningful reviewed CT3 framing selected for the existing Feature semantics; established responsibility provenance is preserved.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-D42C14E5}} (line 5132). Working locators are not identity aliases.
