\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

Bed-state progression applies the consequences of relevant clinical and environmental events to the managed place state. The resulting change is an operational fact, such as a need for cleaning after departure, rather than a transfer of clinical responsibility.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Progress bed states in response to clinical and environmental events (e.g., patient discharge automatically transitions bed to \texttt{\seqsplit{DIRTY}}).


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Meaningful reviewed CT3 framing selected for the existing Feature semantics; established responsibility provenance is preserved.


