\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Curate associations to information and binary content needed to interpret and use a clinical record, retaining custody and source-authority distinctions.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Reviewed candidate}

Curate associations to information and binary content needed to interpret and use a clinical record, retaining custody and source-authority distinctions.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Association is not physical custody. Persistence authority, source clinical meaning and external repository authority remain separate.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

Responsibility-preserving placement under the human-reviewed BEC hierarchy; the structural assertion remains Proposed.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Review Confidence}
Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:0c75887c024354f6]{sylloge-binary-content-management.md:14}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Associate, resolve, retrieve and assemble binary content needed to use managed clinical or operational information.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Logical information may refer to one or several payloads held internally or by an external custodian. This capability keeps association and custody knowledge explicit so that content can be obtained under the governing information contract.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Obtain the content needed to use a managed information item without assuming where every payload is physically held.


