\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

A logical clinical item may reference externally held or multipart payloads. The Feature supplies a usable content result while retaining custody and missing-content standing.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition — Proposed}

Resolve governed payload associations and retrieve or assemble the content required by a requesting information context.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Boundary}

No assumption of local copying, shared storage, universal content retention or originating clinical authority.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

This behaviour changes or exposes the bounded concern of Associated Clinical Binary Content Enablement, rather than inheriting an adjacent responsibility.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:0c75887c024354f6]{sylloge-binary-content-management.md:14}
