\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Function Overview}

Retrieval obtains discrete clinical information or attachments under the owning access responsibility. It is distinct from applying the access-qualified filtering required by FEAT-ISE-09. A shared owner and related data do not justify making that unresolved realisation association authoritative.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

Fetches discrete clinical observations and original attachments.


\emph{Feature association not established}: \texttt{\seqsplit{FEAT-ISE-09 — Access-Controlled Information Filtering}} requires access-controlled disclosure/\allowbreak{}filtering; retrieval of discrete information alone does not materially realise that responsibility. No replacement Feature is assigned.


