\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Maintain source attribution and meaningful transformation lineage for health information managed across care boundaries.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Recipients need to know which assertions were received, transformed or superseded and why. This ability preserves those meaningful relationships without making every retry or active-state reconstruction permanent provenance.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Allow a reader to explain the meaningful source and transformation history of a managed assertion.


