Medium; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e0aea98a63ef9e8e]{calliope-models-and-datasets.md:120}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Reviewed reconciliation provenance}
Reconciliation against the explicit human-reviewed BEC candidate hierarchy. Bounded semantic reconciliation; no unconstrained synthesis \hyperref[evidence:405e9742dcba8b45]{reviewed-bec-hierarchy.json:2}
\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Manage the approved runtime content and revision standing of healthcare reference datasets.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Value-set membership, mapping content and governed nomenclature may change independently of the structural definition that gives them meaning. Updates need identifiable review and effective standing without redefining model libraries as mutable data.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Make approved reference-content change usable during operation without changing the meaning of its structural definition.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{BEC-43B6CE64}} (line 9123). Working locators are not identity aliases.
