\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Feature Overview}

A model definition can remain stable while approved terminology membership or mapping content changes. This Feature represents that operational governance without making every definition runtime mutable.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Definition — Proposed}

Review, accept and expose authorised changes to mutable reference content with effective revision standing.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Boundary}

Does not invent an approval authority or bypass normal durable establishment.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

This behaviour changes or exposes the bounded concern of Governed Reference Dataset Administration, rather than inheriting an adjacent responsibility.


\cataloguefield{paragraph}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from capability-specific behaviour, v0.3 inspection and current architectural evidence. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e0aea98a63ef9e8e]{calliope-models-and-datasets.md:120}
