\cataloguefield{subsection}{Pre-review semantics — historical}

Exact prior assertions are retained as reconciliation evidence, rather than descriptions of the current reviewed capability.


\textbf{Previous definition:} Assemble and release existing health information for an explicitly authorised research purpose under applicable use constraints.


\textbf{Previous overview:} Research support must retain the purpose, applicable approvals and release qualification of supplied information. It reuses governed retrieval and privacy controls rather than claiming a clinical-trial or research-governance platform.


\textbf{Previous intent:} Supply the permitted existing information for a particular authorised research use.


