\cataloguefield{section}{Capability Overview}

Entity integrity, context, lifecycle, information maintenance, discovery and semantic conformance are constituent reusable abilities; none is an implementation subsystem.


\cataloguefield{section}{Definition — Proposed}

Maintain identifiable, meaningful, context-qualified and retrievable information through valid state progression.


\cataloguefield{section}{Intent}

Keep information identity, meaning, context, state and retrieval compatible across diverse healthcare uses.


\cataloguefield{section}{Boundary}

Information management and semantic governance do not grant originating domain authority or erase active/\allowbreak{}durable state separation.


\cataloguefield{section}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:27549d51551beae6]{architectural-axioms.md:668}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{section}{Prior Candidate Derivation}
\hyperref[model:reconciliation]{v0.3 reconciliation}: \texttt{\seqsplit{EC-BBAD8E2C}} (line 9792); \texttt{\seqsplit{EC-47C59623}} (line 10023); \texttt{\seqsplit{EC-1F33C0E8}} (line 10668). Working locators are not identity aliases.
\cataloguefield{section}{Scope / Contained Elements}
\begingroup\small\setlength{\TableWidth}{\dimexpr\linewidth-6\tabcolsep-4\arrayrulewidth\relax}
\begin{longtable}{|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.52\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.2\TableWidth}|>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.28\TableWidth}|}
\hline\rowcolor{TableHead}\textbf{Element / page} &amp; \textbf{Type / tier} &amp; \textbf{Element / placement status}\\\hline\endfirsthead
