\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

The semantic execution envelope applies to one-step and multi-step activity and stays distinct from dispatch and supervision.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Define the context requirements, expected outcomes and housekeeping of an operational undertaking.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Intent}

Keep the semantic promise of an undertaking separate from the machinery that executes it.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

A fulfilment definition does not execute, orchestrate or choreograph its activity.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:ea0c62dfd5edfd4a]{context-and-persistence-management.md:52}; \hyperref[evidence:ec6250f7cf7c29a5]{DesignNote-Digital-Twin-Behaviour-and-Execution-Semantics.md:73}
