\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Interaction \&amp; Experience makes contextual information and governed actions available to human participants through presentation and collaboration integration. Clinical timelines, directory administration and operational dashboards have different purposes, but share a need to retain established identity, security and information context. The recurring responsibility is usable interaction within those boundaries.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

\begin{itemize}

\item
\textbf{Architectural Scope}: Provide contextual interaction between human actors, Harmonia, and enterprise presentation services, including visualization, alerting, and collaboration integration.



\item
\textbf{Functional Responsibilities}:


\begin{itemize}

\item
Mediating presentation interactions via dedicated backend-for-frontend gateways decoupled from internal databases.



\item
Rendering clinical timelines, provider directory management interfaces, and operational console dashboards.



\item
Providing contextual notifications and alerts to human users across web and mobile channels.



\item
Projecting longitudinal record context into secure multidisciplinary collaboration spaces.



\end{itemize}


\item
\textbf{Boundary Note}: Does not absorb the healthcare semantics of Clinical Collaboration or medical documentation. Consumes established identity and security context; does not own authentication, consent, or clinical truth.



\end{itemize}

\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Presentation does not own consent, authentication or clinical truth, and collaboration projection does not absorb clinical documentation semantics.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Proposed Placement Rationale}

The established reusable responsibility is a constituent ability of Coordinated Activity \&amp; Interaction; its canonical scope and exclusions remain unchanged.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Relationships / Architectural Relevance}
