\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Capability Overview}

Permission depends on controlled criteria, role assignments, action and information scope; revocation is distinct from natural expiry.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Resolve effective, temporally applicable permission criteria for an established identity and governed operation.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Intent}

Determine the effective permitted action under the applicable identity, information and temporal criteria.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Boundary}

Does not authenticate identity or grant permission from caller-controlled tags or mere role names.


\cataloguefield{subsubsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:13afd583ac468df7]{DesignNote-Identity-Authentication-and-Authorisation-Architecture.md:33}
\Needspace{8\baselineskip}
\subsection{Enterprise CT3: Operation-Bound Policy Enforcement}
\label{cap:ec-operation-bound-policy-enforcement}
\index{Operation-Bound Policy Enforcement}
\begingroup\small\setlength{\TableWidth}{\dimexpr\linewidth-6\tabcolsep-4\arrayrulewidth\relax}
