HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: Canonical assurance against a governed subject is not independent review of the assurance service itself.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Function Overview}

Adjudication establishes the supported finding or conclusion from assessed detail. It is distinct from gathering evidence and from reporting an outcome already reached. Insufficiency must remain explicit rather than be forced into satisfaction or non-satisfaction, and the resulting finding does not acquire authority to remediate the subject.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition / governed semantic detail}

\begin{itemize}

\item
\textbf{Canonical Name}: \texttt{\seqsplit{Adjudicate Assurance Assessment}}.



\item
\textbf{Definition}: Determines the assurance finding or conclusion that follows from the assessed evidence and applicable assurance criteria.



\item
\textbf{Boundary}: Establishment of the finding/\allowbreak{}conclusion is part of adjudication. It remains distinct from evidence assessment, operational response, remediation, escalation, workflow progression and clinical judgement. No separate conclusion-establishment or reporting Function is introduced merely because a conclusion is established or may be communicated.



\end{itemize}

\cataloguefield{subsection}{Preserved v0.1 Review Matters}

No contextual-view placement is established.


