\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

An identifiable physical device carries UDI and serial context through its use. The instance record supports association and resolution without originating device observations or making maintenance decisions.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Tracking physical device hardware instances and serial numbers.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Keep the identity of the actual physical equipment distinguishable from its model and endpoint.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Identifies physical hardware; serial tracking is distinct from maintenance and live observation content.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:e01893359d483acf]{business-enabling-capabilities.md:222}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Reviewed successors}
\nameref{cap:bec-device-definition} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-device-definition})
