\cataloguefield{subsection}{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED}

HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: The previous grouping frames Canonical subject-assurance execution; it cannot be equated with review of the assurance service itself.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Associate trustworthy evidence, assess it and adjudicate independently reportable findings about governed service behaviour. Its constituent abilities distinguish Governed Assurance.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Associate trustworthy evidence, assess it and adjudicate independently reportable findings about governed service behaviour.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Produce findings supported by applicable evidence and criteria while retaining inability to conclude.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

The subject can supply evidence but cannot control its conclusion. Evidence insufficiency remains distinct from execution uncertainty and clinical judgement.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:4bac85accd34ce0b]{business-architecture-metamodel.md:49}; \hyperref[evidence:be61392fefb4bb10]{information-responsibility.md:10}
