\cataloguefield{subsection}{HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED}

HUMAN ADJUDICATION REQUIRED: Requirement publication/\allowbreak{}authority is not assurance-service review or information-model design; the reviewed hierarchy does not allocate a home.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Capability Overview}

Consumers need an identifiable statement of which rule applies and who established it. This proposal fills BC-17 information support without giving the platform authority to make legislation, approve governance requirements or reinterpret their force.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Definition — Proposed}

Represent and publish versioned governing requirements for use by authorised operational and assurance consumers.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Intent}

Let operational and assurance consumers identify the governing statement and applicability basis they actually used.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Boundary}

Governance approval remains externally mandated; operational policy, assurance criteria and requirement authority are not interchangeable.


\cataloguefield{subsection}{Review Confidence}
Low; applies to the proposal, not to preserved canonical meaning.
\cataloguefield{subsection}{Derivation Provenance}
Inferred from bounded responsibilities and their semantic decomposition. AI architectural synthesis under the explicitly authorised Step 2 task \hyperref[evidence:a4c0900c47c945d9]{business-capabilities.md:993}; \hyperref[evidence:14c8f26d232fcb78]{health-service-assurance.md:9}
