The responsibility concerns govern the definitions, terminology and reference content that make healthcare information consistently interpretable. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.\\\hline
\nameref{cap:bec-assurance-specification-enablement} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-assurance-specification-enablement}) &amp; \nameref{cap:bec-assurance-design} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-assurance-design}) &amp; Proposed

The responsibility concerns model how satisfaction will be assured and maintain applicable, temporally qualified criteria. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.\\\hline
\nameref{cap:bec-assurance-specification-enablement} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-assurance-specification-enablement}) &amp; \nameref{cap:bec-assurance-criteria-management} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-assurance-criteria-management}) &amp; Proposed

The responsibility concerns model how satisfaction will be assured and maintain applicable, temporally qualified criteria. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.\\\hline
\nameref{cap:bec-independent-assurance-evaluation-enablement} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-independent-assurance-evaluation-enablement}) &amp; \nameref{cap:bec-governed-assurance} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-governed-assurance}) &amp; Historical assertion / Proposed

The responsibility concerns associate trustworthy evidence, assess it and adjudicate independently reportable findings about governed service behaviour. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.\\\hline
\nameref{cap:bec-workforce-qualification-development-enablement} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-workforce-qualification-development-enablement}) &amp; \nameref{cap:bec-credential-management} (p.\,\pageref{cap:bec-credential-management}) &amp; Historical assertion / Proposed

The responsibility concerns represent learning, competence, professional-standing checks and separately governed operational access qualifications. It is the finest capability frame required for the established behaviour; the older contextual heading is not another capability tier.\\\hline
\nameref{cap:ec-governed-information-operations} (p.\,\pageref{cap:ec-governed-information-operations}) &amp; \nameref{cap:ec-01} (p.\,\pageref{cap:ec-01}) &amp; Proposed

The established reusable responsibility is a constituent ability of Governed Information Operations; its canonical scope and exclusions remain unchanged.\\\hline
